It's possible for a barbarian to succumb to fatal poison, but it is by
no means easy even if you are specifically trying to do that.

Read the Guidebook, carefully. Use / and ; liberally. Know when to run
away, and carry a diverse selection of escape magics to help you do
so.

If you want some general advice which is only modestly spoily, the
Absolute Beginner's Guide may fit the bill:
   http://www.melankolia.net/nethack/nethack.guide.html

If you want extremely detailed spoilers about instadeaths only:
   http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/instadeath.html

(Note that the set of stupid ways to die is substantially larger than
the set of instadeaths.)

General barbarian quest advice (so quit reading if you don't want
vague spoilers!): Don't stand next to water you aren't 100% sure is
empty, unless you have an absolute defense against the risks it
poses. Be prepared for lots of straightforward melee. A tinning kit or
ravenous pet is helpful. The nemesis level is teleport-friendly; your
nemesis is a wizard.


